# oxide-sloc — corporate "secure by default" server profile (EXAMPLE)
#
# Copy to deploy/corp.env, edit the values, then launch with everything on:
#
#   set -a; . deploy/corp.env; set +a
#   bash scripts/serve-server.sh            # TLS + auth + rate-limit + CORS, no other flags
#
# …or point the systemd unit at it as an EnvironmentFile (see
# scripts/internal/install-systemd.sh). Every setting below is opt-in; this file
# just turns the good knobs on in one place. These are all environment variables
# (the security surface is env-driven), NOT a --config TOML.
#
# Do NOT commit your filled-in deploy/corp.env — it holds secrets. Only this
# .example belongs in git. (deploy/corp.env is gitignored.)

# ── Bind ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Pin the listen address. Default LAN mode binds 0.0.0.0; set a management-VLAN
# IP here to expose the server on only that interface. --bind overrides this.
#SLOC_BIND=0.0.0.0:4317

# What clients should type in a browser (hostname or IP). Shown as the
# RECOMMENDED URL; use it when DNS / a reverse proxy / NAT means the auto-detected
# LAN IP isn't what people should hit.
#SLOC_ADVERTISE_HOST=sloc.corp.example.com

# ── TLS (HTTPS) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# PEM cert + key enable native HTTPS. Use a CA-issued cert in production; a
# self-signed pair is fine for a first test (clients must trust/accept it).
SLOC_TLS_CERT=/etc/oxide-sloc/tls/server.crt
SLOC_TLS_KEY=/etc/oxide-sloc/tls/server.key
# Refuse to start a cleartext non-loopback listener (belt-and-suspenders with the
# certs above). Uncomment to hard-require TLS.
#SLOC_REQUIRE_TLS=1
# Optional mutual TLS: require clients to present a cert signed by this CA.
#SLOC_TLS_CLIENT_CA=/etc/oxide-sloc/tls/client-ca.crt

# ── Authentication ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Full-access API keys (comma-separated). Generate with: openssl rand -hex 32
SLOC_API_KEYS=replace-with-a-long-random-secret
# Read-only keys: authenticate GET/HEAD/OPTIONS only; rejected on writes.
#SLOC_API_KEYS_READONLY=replace-with-another-random-secret
# Brute-force lockout: N failures from one IP → temporary block for M seconds.
SLOC_AUTH_LOCKOUT_FAILS=10
SLOC_AUTH_LOCKOUT_SECS=3600
# Set secure cookies (recommended when serving over HTTPS).
SLOC_SECURE_COOKIES=1
# Idle session timeout in seconds (auto-logout).
#SLOC_SESSION_IDLE_SECS=1800

# ── Rate limiting ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Requests per minute per client IP (server-mode default is 120). Lower on a
# shared/hostile segment; raise for trusted automation.
SLOC_RATE_LIMIT=120
# Behind a reverse proxy, trust X-Forwarded-For so limits are per-client, not
# per-proxy. Set the proxy's IP(s) or the limiter buckets everyone together.
#SLOC_TRUST_PROXY=1
#SLOC_TRUSTED_PROXY_IPS=10.0.0.2

# ── CORS ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Comma-separated origins allowed to make cross-origin browser API calls. Unset
# = same-origin only (no Access-Control-Allow-Origin emitted).
#SLOC_ALLOWED_ORIGINS=https://portal.corp.example.com,https://ci.corp.example.com

# ── Embedding (only if the UI must live in a corp dashboard) ─────────────────
# Space-separated origins permitted to iframe the UI. Rewrites CSP frame-ancestors
# and X-Frame-Options. Unset = default-deny (cannot be framed anywhere).
#SLOC_FRAME_ANCESTORS=https://portal.corp.example.com

# ── Scan scope ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Directories the web UI may scan (colon-separated absolute paths).
# In SERVER mode this is FAIL-CLOSED: while it is UNSET, every server-side path
# scan is rejected with HTTP 403 — nothing under the host filesystem is scannable.
# Set it to the repos you want analyzable to enable server-side path scans.
# (The Browse / directory-upload flow always works — uploads are scanned from the
# server's temp area and bypass this allowlist.)  Required on a shared host.
#SLOC_ALLOWED_ROOTS=/srv/repos:/home/ci/work

# ── Audit logging (tamper-evident) ──────────────────────────────────────────
# Append security events as JSON lines for SIEM ingestion.
SLOC_AUDIT_LOG=/var/log/oxide-sloc/audit.jsonl
# Keyed HMAC secret → hash-chains each record so edits/reorders/truncation are
# detectable. Generate with: openssl rand -hex 32
SLOC_AUDIT_HMAC_KEY=replace-with-a-long-random-secret
#SLOC_AUDIT_LOG_MAX_MB=10
#SLOC_AUDIT_LOG_KEEP=5

# ── Consent banner (optional) ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# Show an acknowledgement banner on first load (e.g. authorized-use notice).
#SLOC_CONSENT_BANNER=Authorized use only. Activity is monitored and logged.

# ── Canonical hostname (let LAN users use a name, not an IP) ─────────────────
# The URL clients use. Printed at startup with a DNS-resolution check plus the
# exact A-record / hosts-file line to add. The app does NOT edit host DNS itself.
#SLOC_PUBLIC_URL=https://sloc.corp.example.com

# Host-header allowlist (anti DNS-rebinding / Host injection). When set, requests
# with any other Host get 421. The SLOC_PUBLIC_URL host is auto-trusted; health,
# metrics, and webhook paths are exempt. Comma- or space-separated.
#SLOC_ALLOWED_HOSTS=sloc.corp.example.com,10.20.0.5

# ── Disk ceiling (garbage collection) ───────────────────────────────────────
# Hard cap (MB) on total retained scan artifacts. A background guard deletes the
# oldest runs over this; uploads are refused 507 when staging is full; the in-UI
# cleanup policy can only tighten below it.
#SLOC_MAX_DISK_MB=20000

# ── Off-box report publishing (export targets) ──────────────────────────────
# Per run: POST /api/runs/{id}/export?target=<share|git|confluence>
# 1) Mounted network / SMB share:
#SLOC_EXPORT_DIR=/mnt/reports-share
#SLOC_EXPORT_AUTO=1                 # auto-publish every finished scan to the share
# 2) Git repository (per-run subdir, pushed to a branch; reuses git creds/SSRF gates):
#SLOC_EXPORT_GIT_REPO=https://git.corp.example.com/team/sloc-reports.git
#SLOC_EXPORT_GIT_BRANCH=oxide-sloc-reports
# 3) Confluence: configure at /integrations (uses the existing Confluence integration)

# ── Operator admin key ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Separate credential (distinct from user API keys) required for the operator
# effective-config view: GET /api/admin/config. Generate with: openssl rand -hex 32
#SLOC_ADMIN_KEY=replace-with-a-long-random-secret
